From 347878353595bf2e21c1f7c92f594e757756940e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:26:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Android: the logcat thread reads its pipe with read(), not
 fgets on a FILE*

fgets held the reader stream's lock while it waited for a line, so every fflush(nullptr) in the process
(the memory card's, after each write) waited for the next log line, about a second: a card format crawled
at one page per second and the game looked frozen. Ps2LinePump (runtime/ps2_log_pump.h) splits the bytes
into lines; ps2PumpLines reads the descriptor. Tests: LogPump (3).
---
